From e0a17f3aa543cf5cb82bd157ff8837f063c0f26e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jacob Oursland <jacob.oursland@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 00:50:31 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 07/18] solidcore-step: assemble a B-rep record from loose
 faces, edges and vertices, whatever file they came from

The STEP reader's second half (seams on periodic surfaces, frames turned so a round face's form
covers it once, edge labels and NURBS forms, pcurves, outer loops and face sides, tolerances
raised to the geometry's gaps, regions and the canonical order) moves out of `topology` into a
format-neutral `assembly` module. A reader adds vertices, edges on curves and faces on surfaces
with their bounds through `Assembly::add_vertex`, `add_edge` and `add_face`, then calls
`Assembly::finish`. The STEP reader now does exactly that; spline construction from full knot
vectors (`spline_curve`, `spline_surface`, with exact clamping) moves with it.

This is the first step of reading FreeCAD and Rhino files through cadmpeg's neutral model
(CADIR) straight into records instead of through STEP text: that reader needs the same
finishing, and one implementation of it.

No behaviour changes for STEP: solidcore-step's 104 tests pass as on main. `add_edge` decides
an edge's direction from its geometry (STEP keeps its own same_sense handling), and three new
tests build a box through the API alone. The moved panic sites keep their rows, re-keyed.

