From 2c4456c93eae887152884072d0d94830b4f4a83f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jacob Oursland <jacob.oursland@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 11:33:09 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 08/18] solidcore-step: a sphere bounded by its poles is whole
 in the shared assembly; spline constructors refuse malformed values

Review follow-up. A sphere face bounded by vertex loops at its poles alone became the whole ball
only in the STEP reader (`whole_sphere`); any other reader adding the same bounds through
`Assembly::add_face` had the face refused. The completion moves into `Assembly`, which both use.
`spline_curve` and `spline_surface` now refuse knots that are not finite or decrease, an empty
parameter domain, non-finite control points and weights that are not positive, instead of
returning them.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../crates/solidcore-step/src/assembly.rs     | 75 ++++++++++++++++++-
 .../solidcore-step/src/assembly_tests.rs      | 39 ++++++++++
 .../crates/solidcore-step/src/topology.rs     | 38 +---------
 3 files changed, 114 insertions(+), 38 deletions(-)

