From 38e6e9ed71339e7c37001fd23d634baf6de5ae69 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jacob Oursland <jacob.oursland@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 12:41:35 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 12/18] solidcore-cadir: edges across a periodic spline's seam,
 and parabola and hyperbola edges

Review follow-up.
- An edge on a spline CADIR marks periodic may have an interval past the spline's range or
  across its seam (CADIR evaluates it modulo its period). The interval is moved into the range by
  whole periods, and the curve restarted there when the edge crosses the seam, exactly as the
  STEP reader reads such an edge (`assembly::periodic_edge`). Before, such an edge was read on
  the clamped spline and refused for a vertex off its curve.
- Parabola and hyperbola edges, which the STEP route brought in through STEP's PARABOLA and
  HYPERBOLA and this reader refused, are the STEP reader's exact conic splines over each edge's
  interval (`assembly::parabola_curve`, `hyperbola_curve`); CADIR's parameters for both are
  STEP's.
- Tests: a degree-one periodic square read across its seam is at (5, 0, 0) at parameter 4.5;
  parabola and hyperbola edges end on their conics.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
