From d4ee78b40862c034942f4d0a139777881b51a608 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jacob Oursland <jacob.oursland@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 03:18:58 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 15/18] FreeCAD and Rhino import: read the file's solids
 straight into B-rep records, with no STEP text in between

Opening, inserting or dropping a FreeCAD .FCStd or Rhino .3dm file used to have cadmpeg write
the file's neutral model out as STEP text, which the STEP reader then read back and the design
kept. Now the neutral model (CADIR) is read straight into B-rep records by solidcore-cadir, and
the Import feature keeps those records. The same bodies come in: on every FreeCAD and Rhino file
in the tests the records route builds the same bodies as the STEP route did, with the same faces,
volumes (to 1e-12), extents and centres, the knob's body placement included.

What changes:
- FreeCAD's hidden intermediate shapes are left out from the model's own visibility, not from
  INVISIBILITY entities parsed back out of STEP text; a Rhino object keeps its own name.
- The STEP round trip and its fixes are gone: `native_cad_to_step`, the INVISIBILITY scan and the
  renaming of cadmpeg's placeholder product. cadmpeg's STEP codec stays compiled in for reading.
- solidcore-cadir reports each body's rigid placement; a placement that scales is left out with
  a warning, as cadmpeg's STEP writer did.
- Body colours are not brought over yet (the STEP route brought none): a Rhino object's colour
  is often its layer's default black, which is not how Rhino shades it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
